    "The movie *Lean on Me* was primarily filmed in **East St. Louis, Illinois**. \n\nSpecifically, the high school featured in the film is **Lincoln High School** (now Lincoln Middle School). Much of the movie was shot on location *inside* the actual school while classes were in session!\n\nSome additional filming also took place in **nearby areas of St. Louis, Missouri**, but East St. Louis and Lincoln High School were the main locations.",
    "The movie *Lean on Me* was primarily filmed in **East St. Louis, Illinois**. \n\nSpecifically, the high school featured in the film is **Lincoln High School** (now Lincoln Middle School). Much of the movie was shot on location there and in the surrounding East St. Louis area to authentically portray the challenges faced by the school and community.\n\nSome additional filming also took place in **St. Louis, Missouri**, which is very close to East St. Louis.",
    "The movie *Lean on Me* was primarily filmed in **Passaic, New Jersey**. \n\nSpecifically, **Eastside High School** in Passaic was used as the main location for the film, standing in for the fictional Eastside High School where Joe Clark (played by Morgan Freeman) was principal.\n\nWhile some scenes were also shot in other parts of New Jersey, Passaic and Eastside High are the most recognizable and significant filming locations."
